  {
    "key": "text_209",
    "value": "Book your stay at Neskapolita in Juay\u00faa\u2014the perfect, central base for all your western mountain adventures.",
    "files": [
      "src/imports/RutaFloresMapPageDesktop/index.tsx"
    ]
  },
  {
    "key": "text_210",
    "value": "How many days do you need for Ruta de las Flores?",
    "files": [
      "src/imports/RutaFloresMapPageDesktop/index.tsx"
    ]
  },
  {
    "key": "text_211",
    "value": "We recommend 2 to 3 days to fully explore the food markets, hike to waterfalls, and tour coffee farms at a relaxed highland pace.",
    "files": [
      "src/imports/RutaFloresMapPageDesktop/index.tsx"
    ]
  },
  {
    "key": "text_212",
    "value": "What is the best town to visit in Ruta de las Flores?",
    "files": [
      "src/imports/RutaFloresMapPageDesktop/index.tsx"
    ]
  },
  {
    "key": "text_213",
    "value": "Juay\u00faa is the perfect culinary and adventure hub, while Ataco shines with its street art, and Apaneca offers high-altitude nature.",
    "files": [
      "src/imports/RutaFloresMapPageDesktop/index.tsx"
    ]
  },
  {
    "key": "text_214",
    "value": "Can you visit Ruta de las Flores without a car?",
    "files": [
      "src/imports/RutaFloresMapPageDesktop/index.tsx"
    ]
  },
  {
    "key": "text_215",
    "value": "What is the best time of year to visit Ruta de las Flores?",
    "files": [
      "src/imports/RutaFloresMapPageDesktop/index.tsx"
    ]
  },
  {
    "key": "text_216",
    "value": "The dry season from November to April offers beautiful sunny weather, but the green season (May to October) makes waterfalls spectacular.",
